---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin page
    participant Api as Export routes<br/>/api/export<br/>/api/export/status/[jobId]
    participant Job as Background job<br/>zip export
    participant DB as Supabase DB
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant Store as Supabase Storage<br/>gpx-tracks bucket

    Note over Admin,Store: Covers US 3.0.3. The flow copies the PDF job pattern<br/>(S26_pdf_jobs, after(), presigned URL).<br/>export_jobs is like S26_pdf_jobs, without mode and request_payload.

    Admin->>Page: Select Export all files
    Page->>Api: POST /api/export
    Api->>Api: Check caller is Admin: app_metadata role is admin<br/>and the account is approved
    alt Caller is not Admin
        Api-->>Page: 403. No job is made
        Page-->>Admin: Show "not allowed"
    else Caller is Admin and has an export that started in the last 30 minutes<br/>and is still pending or processing
        Api-->>Page: 409 with that jobId. No new job is made
        Page->>Page: Follow the job that is already running
    else Caller is Admin
        Api->>DB: Insert export_jobs row,<br/>status pending, created_by = caller
        Api-->>Page: 202 with jobId
        Api->>Job: after(): run zip job
        Job->>DB: Read storage keys page by page from attachments,<br/>homepage_image_uploads, gpx_tracks<br/>and completed S26_pdf_jobs
        DB-->>Job: Storage keys
        loop Each stored file, one at a time
            alt Image or PDF
                Job->>S3: Get file
                S3-->>Job: File
            else GPX track
                Job->>Store: Download file
                Store-->>Job: File
            end
            Job->>Job: Add file to zip. Stop when the files total more than 500 MB
        end
        alt A file is missing, the files total more than 500 MB, or the job fails
            Job->>DB: Update export_jobs row: status failed,<br/>error with the file names (up to 10) or the 500 MB limit
        else Zip is made (AT 1, AT 2)
            Job->>S3: Put zip file
            Job->>DB: Update export_jobs row: status complete,<br/>storage_path of the zip
        end
        Page->>Api: GET /api/export/status/[jobId]
        Api->>Api: Check session. Check caller is Admin or job creator
        alt Caller is not Admin and not the job creator
            Api-->>Page: 403. No status and no URL
        else Caller is allowed
            Api->>DB: Read export_jobs row
            DB-->>Api: status, error, storage_path
            alt Status is failed
                Api-->>Page: Failed with error
                Page-->>Admin: Show Failed with reason
            else Status is pending or processing
                Api-->>Page: Not ready
                Page-->>Admin: Show progress and ask again later
            else Status is complete
                Api-->>Page: Presigned download URL
                Page-->>Admin: Download ZIP with all images, GPX files and completed PDFs
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Job,Store: One export holds at most 500 MB. The job builds the zip in memory,<br/>so a larger limit needs a multipart upload.
